==Strategy==
If you're confident with your strategy or have already beaten the stage and are willing to spend 2 Cat CPUs, you may want to bring a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]] for the one-time 10,000,000 XP drop.

This stage is incredibly difficult without [[True Form]]s of [[Uncanny Legends]] [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] like [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]] and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]. One should True Form Ancient Egg: N000 before attempting the stage without suitable [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]], as they make Magamojoe much easier to handle. Needless to say, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] are almost a must if you do not want to cheese the stage or use Ubers. Below is a general strategy to clear the stage.

#Push Metafilibuster all the way to the enemy base before Magamojoe appears. This can be done by using both Courier Cat and Mushroom Cat. This step is relatively straightforward if you can push Cumulus Gallus (using [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] or otherwise) and keep Angelic Beast Rajakong in check with Mushroom Cat and good meatshielding as well as a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] of your choice. Bring the [[Ototo Corps|Iron Wall Cannon]] to hold the peons when Angelic Beast Rajakong's boss shockwave occurs. Note: Don't kill Cumulus too fast. Instead, try to deplete some of Rajakong's HP, since [[Ancient Magamojoe|Magamojoe]] will appear once Cumulus is killed.
#When Magamojoe appears, stall for a short moment and let Metafilibuster kill all your units, make sure that you bring a unit that can survive a hit, like [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]], Macho Crystal Cat, or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] so as to re-trigger Metafilibuster's attack animation and keep him at the enemy base for another 45 seconds. Bring Ancient Magamojoe (and Angelic Beast Rajakong or Cumulus Gallus if either are not dead at this moment) close to the base and keep Ancient Magamojoe at approximately 400 range from your base. This allows for your expensive units to not get hit by Metafilibuster's next hit.
#You will have anywhere from about 50 to about 100 seconds to reach and hit Metafilibuster depending on the position of Ancient Magamojoe when Metafilibuster is first hit, how you knock Ancient Magamojoe back and if you can trigger his attack again without getting the base hit. You will therefore need a minimum of 22000 DPS on Ancient Magamojoe through whatever means necessary. Alternatively, you can do some maths with your available DPS and clip a fast unit through (with default Cat Cannon/Sniper) to give yourself more time.

On higher difficulty clears, this stage plays almost exactly the same given that you now have access to [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] and the minimal gains from higher difficulties.
===Super Tough Mission===
The Super Tough Mission requires you to use 9+ Rare cats. Here, Cat Egg Pod is pretty much mandatory here, as it can effectively stall the Behemoth of the stage, especially Ancient Magamojoe. Awakened Naala is the preferred non-Rare cat of choice, as they have strong piercing damage to juggle Metafilibuster and has strong damage output against the Behemoths of the stage, particularly Magamojoe.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]]: When Talented with Massive Damage, Attack Buff and Defense Buff, this unit can quickly remove the Ragin' Gories.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier's Behemoth Slayer is useful against most enemies here, and can quickly remove Casaurian Ahirujo from play, but might require a fair bit of support to work against other Behemoths.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Mushroom has Behemoth Slayer and Massive Damage to Angels, which allows it to quickly cripple and defeat Angelic Beast Rajakong with its superior range and Wave Immunity.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]: Naala is able to outrange most of the pushers here save for Cumulus Gallus and Ancient Magamojoe with its Behemoth Slayer while being Strong Against Relics and Curse Immunity makes Magamojoe much more manageable. Its immunity to Waves and Surges are notable against both Magamojoe and Rajakong. Its LD hits up to 700 range, too, and can potentially reach Metafilibuster from all these threats.
*Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Have a power to obliterate nearly everything here. Can rips enemies health as usual, knockback Metafilibuster (as he isn't immune to explosion) and easily chains Cumulus with support from other units and Attack Combo. The only enemy that isn't victim of his apocalypse are Magamoejoe as his multi-hit and Surge attack are unmatched for Bahamut.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: To trigger Metafilibuster's attack without having him even advance.
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]: Ape Lord Luza's Massive Damage and Resistance to Relics, Behemoth Slayer as well as Curse and Surge Immunity makes it particularly suited to neutralizing Magamojoe.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]]: Can be use as Luza replacement if you don't have him. Though function differently, she's still used to deal significant damage to Magamoejoe. Try to timed her properly as she might get hit from Magamoejoe's multi-hit attack or hit Gory instead.
*[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: Players who have cleared all Behemoth Culling stages can consider using Cat Egg Pod as a tanker here, as most of the threats are Behemoths. With high HP, one Knockback, a wide assortment of Immunities and Behemoth Slayer further boosting its defensive capabilities (50% chance to Dodge Behemoths for 2 seconds, rather than the usual 5% chance to Dodge for 1 second), it can hold off the nasty Behemoths for quite a while as other attackers catch up.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
* [[Assassinlan Pasalan]]: With such a long range, it can snipe Metafilibuster super easily.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]]: Counters Ancient Magamojoe and [[Casaurian Ahirujo]].
*[[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventure Girl Kanna]]: Can work in a similar fashion to Naala, though only has [[Behemoth Slayer]] and massive damage against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies to counter the Ragin' Gories. Her third hit goes up to 1000 range, allowing her to easily hit Metafilibuster and interrupt him.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Yukimura's very high speed makes him easier to clip through Magamojoe and hit Metafilibuster if you need some additional time, should you try it. He also comes into use when dealing with the Ragin' Gories.
*[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Count Yukimura]]: Count Yukimura does the same job as normal Yukimura, but has higher speed for easier clipping and massive damage for floating for chip on Metafilibuster. Though normal Yukimura is still better for the Ragin' Gories.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunacia]]: While Lunacia only targets the two behemoth birds, her freeze is extremely helpful against Magamojoe, allowing Courier and other behemoth slayers to sneak in hits towards him. She also has decent dps, especially against Magamojoe, and her explosions may be able to snipe Metafilibuster himself which can reset his foreswing.

